// FB-007 regression pin (Rust differential feedback, sla-plugin-rust
// docs/feedback/FB-007): emitPrintln measured literal format-string
// segments with the RAW source span (escape sequences counted as
// backslash + letter) while the emitted @const utf8 data stores the
// escape-EVALUATED bytes, so the text backend printed past the end of
// every escape-bearing segment (observed pre-fix stdout for the first
// println below: "a\nb\tc" followed by two over-read bytes from the
// adjacent constants, and the "x\ny=" segment swallowing the "!" of
// the next segment, printing it before the interpolated value). The
// string-argument path and format() already used the evaluated byte
// length; segments now do too. Corpus tests cannot assert on stdout,
// so this file pins the shapes as compile+run clean on both backends;
// the byte-level before/after evidence (generated .sa lengths and
// od -c stdout dumps) is recorded in the fix line's RESULT.md.
@test "fb007 println escape segments stay in bounds"() {
    println("a\nb\tc");
    println("x\ny={}!", 42);
    println("plain");
    let s = format("q\t{}", 7);
    if !str_eq(s, "q\t7") { panic(74607); };
}
